LRC n=16 Cayley-Dickson proof attempt (codex-2026-05-31 S389)
n=16 means k=15 moving speeds and threshold 1/16.

Cayley-Dickson dictionary:
  doubling layer      -> dyadic quotient layer
  norm conservation   -> gap/debt ledger
  dimension-16 zero divisor -> 16-gate protecting old units but leaking
  lost alternativity  -> labelled endpoint cycle must be checked, not
                         just the projected support cycle

UNIT-GATE LEMMA
==============================================================================
For odd a, the unit endpoint t=a/16 can be strictly protected by
speed v only if v*a == 0 mod 16, hence only if 16 divides v.
This gives a real first branch of a proof attempt:
  no 16-multiple -> an odd a/16 endpoint is a boundary witness.

  v=16 protects odd unit endpoints [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15]
  v=32 protects odd unit endpoints [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15]

