radius=2: checked=378000 best_missed=160 best_count=16 positions=(10, 15) deltas=(8,)
  first_example=(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 8)

Interpretation:
  The best one-defect is a half-turn in the last coordinate, missing
  128 cells.  The best two-defect still misses 160 cells.  This is the
  finite scalar moat a full n=16 proof would need to lift from the
  normalized residue model back to arbitrary primitive speed sets.

