PROOF ATTEMPT STATUS
==============================================================================
A plausible n=16 proof now has this shape:
  1. No 16-gate is impossible for a counterexample by the unit-gate lemma.
  2. A 16-gate closes the old unit skeleton only by exporting endpoint
     debt to v2-denominator layers 5,6,7,8.  The dyadic ladders preserve
     a positive debt norm instead of approaching an open cover.
  3. In the normalized scalar quotient, every one- or two-coordinate
     non-scalar dyadic defect has a large moat.

Missing lemma:
  Every primitive n=16 all-protected endpoint system with a 16-gate
  either descends to one of the dyadic debt ledgers above, or contains
  a labelled endpoint cycle with a private dyadic leaf.  Proving that
  would turn the Cayley-Dickson analogy into an actual n=16 proof.
